0.001001,"pass_rate":0.4821,"pass_rate_neutral":0.4583,"def_epa_per_play":0.4604},{"week":3,"opponent":"KC","home":true,"pf":10.0,"pa":24.0,"off_snaps":67,"epa_per_play":-0.1511,"pass_rate":0.5373,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5082,"def_epa_per_play":0.1381},{"week":4,"opponent":"MIN","home":false,"pf":10.0,"pa":15.0,"off_snaps":37,"epa_per_play":-0.2039,"pass_rate":0.5135,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5833,"def_epa_per_play":-0.0469},{"week":5,"opponent":"CIN","home":true,"pf":24.0,"pa":31.0,"off_snaps":64,"epa_per_play":-0.03319,"pass_rate":0.4688,"pass_rate_neutral":0.35,"def_epa_per_play":0.1419}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2024,"team":"BAL","distance":0.7947,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Todd Monken"},{"season":2022,"team":"CHI","distance":0.8194,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"CHI","distance":0.8205,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"BAL","distance":0.8215,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Todd Monken"},{"season":2023,"team":"SF","distance":0.8548,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kyle Shanahan"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"LV","distance":0.2921,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Patrick Graham"},{"season":2022,"team":"HOU","distance":0.3218,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"BAL","distance":0.3767,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Mike Macdonald"},{"season":2025,"team":"TEN","distance":0.3806,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennard Wilson"},{"season":2024,"team":"NO","distance":0.4412,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Dolphins are 0-5 through week 6 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 132 to 70. Neither side has held up so far, with the offense 28th in EPA per play and the defense 29th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive trait is the lowest pass rate over expected in the league.","offense":"The Dolphins offense has struggled, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. They have been one of the most run-heavy teams in the league, passing less often than game situations would predict. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 2nd highest pre-snap motion rate in the league. Malik Willis has run the passing game and leaned heavily on Malik Washington, who has drawn 28% of the targets.","defense":"The Dolphins have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 29th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per rush, where it ranks 9th, and its weakest has been sack rate, where it ranks 32nd. Zach Sieler has led the way with 2 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is a number of defenders in the box that ranks 5th highest in the league.","special":"The Dolphins have been one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 62% of their short-yardage chances so far. Their kickers have made 78% of field goals, which is a little below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into running backs, about 11% of the money on the books. Their running backs were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Malik Willis has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 849 yards. Malik Washington has been the clear top target with 28% of the looks and 262 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by Ollie Gordon II and De'Von Achane. On defense, Zach Sieler leads the team with 2 sacks.","coaching":"Bobby Slowik is calling the offense and Sean Duggan is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2024 Ravens under Todd Monken and the 2022 Bears. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Raiders under Patrick Graham and the 2022 Texans.","trends":"The offense went from 22nd in EPA per play in 2025 to 28th so far this season, a modest decline. The defense moved from 26th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 29th so far this season, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was fourth down go rate, which went from 18% to 62%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}